cff-version: 1.2.0
message: >-
  If you use RockMin ID in work that you publish, please cite it using the
  metadata below. The DOI here is the concept DOI, which always resolves to the
  latest release; cite it for the software in general. When you need to pin the
  exact release your results were produced with, cite that release's own
  version DOI, which is shown on its Zenodo record.
title: >-
  RockMin ID: Automated Geochemical Classifier and Petrological Analysis
  Platform
abstract: >-
  A deterministic geochemical classifier and petrological analysis platform.
  Rocks and minerals are identified from major-element compositions using a
  full CIPW weight and cation norm, the IUGS total alkali-silica classification
  with its sub-root naming rules, the published Irvine & Baragar (1971)
  discriminant equations, ten ternary projections, and structural-formula
  (APFU) mineral identification. Reference distributions are derived from the
  full GEOROC archives. No AI is involved in classification: every
  identification, field assignment and index is a reproducible, unit-tested
  calculation. Runs entirely in the browser, installs as a PWA, and works
  offline.
type: software
